                "ORA_LAYOUT_MESSAGES_LIST"
              ],
              "enableActions": true,
              "enableCommunications": true,
              "customNotes": "Render the JSON array teamTalent as a messageListWidget. Sort employees who need adjustment first. For each item, emit a complete messageListWidget row with these display fields:\n\n{\n  \"title\": teamTalent.title,\n  \"subtitle\": teamTalent.ratingDescription,\n  \"summary\": teamTalent.summary,\n  \"status\": teamTalent.suggestedRating,\n  \"priority\": \"<alert, warning, medium, or success>\",\n  \"image\": \"/hcmUI/personImage?returnSquare=true&returnInitials=Y&removeBackground=Y&personId=<PersonId>&maxSize=44\"\n}\n\nThe subtitle must always be the current manager-rated Overall Summary PerformanceRating description from the OS section. Do not put the recommended rating, worker rating, goal rating, competency rating, or status text in subtitle.\n\nStatus is mandatory for every row. For changed ratings, status must retain the exact format \"Consider adjusting to <recommended-rating>\". For unchanged ratings, status must be exactly \"No change suggested\". Use rating description text only; never use numeric ratings.\n\nDo not emit timestamp. Do not emit badgeText. Do not emit badge, badgePriority, badgeVariant, or any other badge-related field.\n\nOnly include additionalAction when teamTalent.adjustRatingAllowed = Yes, using command ora.Invoke(\"AP\", {\"PersonId\": <PersonId>, \"EvaluationId\": <EvaluationId>, \"context\": \"EDIT\"}) and text \"Adjust\".\n\nShow \"No job associated\" only if JobName is empty. Show \"Unrated\" only when teamTalent.ratingDescription is exactly \"Unrated\" after applying the rating fallback rules."
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {
                "k": 0,
                "max_tokens": 32000,
                "p": 0.75,
                "max_completion_tokens": 32000,
                "reasoning_effort": "low"
              },
              "code": "ORA_MODEL_CONFIG_PREMIUM_OPEN_AI_GPT_4_1_MINI",
