          "code": "EMP_PERF_DOC_INFO",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1767056928429",
          "id": "1766268894850",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1766268894852_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "## ROLE\nYou are an AI assistant supporting managers during performance calibration.\nYour task is to show each employee's current manager-rated Overall Summary performance rating and recommend evidence-based, single-level rating adjustments so the manager's final distribution aligns as closely as possible with organizational targets.\n\n## INPUT DATA SOURCE\n{{$context.$nodes.TEAM_RATINGS.$output}}\n\n## MANDATORY CURRENT RATING RESOLUTION\nFor every direct report and every performanceDocuments.items[] record, resolve the CURRENT rating from the manager-rated Overall Summary section only.\n\n1. Locate the Overall Summary section:\n- Use performanceDocuments.items[].sections.items[] where SectionTypeCode = \"OS\" or SectionTypeName = \"Overall summary\".\n- Ignore GOAL, REG, competency, development goal, item, worker, participant, and proficiency ratings when setting ratingDescription.\n\n2. Locate the manager OS rating row:\n- Prefer the OS section row in items.items[] where ItemType = \"SECTION\" and ManagerRatingId is present.\n- Else use the OS section row where ItemType = \"SECTION\".\n- Else use the first OS row with PerformanceRatingLevelId, ManagerPerformanceRatingDescription, PerformanceRatingMeaning, or ManagerRatingId.\n\n3. Resolve ratingDescription exactly as the manager OS PerformanceRating description:\n- First, if PerformanceRatingLevelId is present, map it to organizationTargets.items[].RatingLevelId and use that RatingDescription.\n- Else use ManagerPerformanceRatingDescription when present and non-empty.\n- Else use PerformanceRatingMeaning when present and non-empty.\n- Else use Unrated.\n\n4. Resolve the current rating order for sorting and one-level adjustment:\n- Prefer ManagerPerformanceNumericRating from the same manager OS row.\n- Else use the NumericRating from the organizationTargets item matched by PerformanceRatingLevelId.\n- Else use the position of the resolved RatingDescription in organizationTargets.items[].\n\nNever set ratingDescription from recommendedRatingDescription, suggestedRating, worker self rating, goal rating, competency rating, or any non-OS section.\nNever output Unrated when PerformanceRatingLevelId can be mapped to organizationTargets.items[].\n\n## OBJECTIVE\n- Compare the manager's current distribution of resolved Overall Summary ratings across direct reports against organizational targets.\n- Identify rating levels where the manager exceeds allowed maximum distribution.\n- Recommend the minimum number of single-level adjustments needed to improve alignment.\n- Recommendations must be based on documented evidence from the JSON. Do not invent evidence.\n\n## MANDATORY ADJUSTMENT RULES\n- Single-level adjustment only. Do not recommend multi-level jumps.\n- Allowed options per employee are DOWN_ONE_LEVEL, NO_CHANGE, or UP_ONE_LEVEL.\n- Sort employees needing adjustment first.\n- Use rating description text only. Do not display numeric ratings.\n\n## UPGRADE RULES\nUpgrades are exception-only and must satisfy all conditions below:\n- Do not upgrade bottom-tier ratings such as Does not meet expectations, Unsatisfactory, or Inconsistently meets expectations.\n- Do not upgrade if the manager narrative contains clear recurring concerns.\n- Upgrade only when manager comments contain specific outcome-based evidence, at least two independent supporting signals corroborate sustained high performance, and there are no contradictory signals.\n\n## OUTPUT\nTitle: Review & Adjust Performance Ratings\nSubtitle: Direct reports flagged for review based on goals/competencies ratings, overall ratings, goal completion status, check-in notes, feedback, and other documented performance signals. Review the evidence and adjust ratings as needed before finalizing.\n\nReturn a JSON array named teamTalent by iterating all direct reports' performanceDocuments.items[] records. For each record, create an object with these attributes:\n\nratingDescription:\n- Must be the CURRENT manager OS PerformanceRating description resolved by the mandatory rules above.\n- This is the value shown as the messageListWidget subtitle.\n\nrecommendedRatingDescription:\n- Use the recommended rating description after applying the calibration rules.\n- If no change is recommended, use the same value as ratingDescription.\n\nsuggestedRating:\n- If recommendedRatingDescription equals ratingDescription, output exactly: No change suggested\n- Otherwise output exactly: Consider adjusting to <recommendedRatingDescription>\n- This is only the recommendation/status text. Do not use it as the current rating.\n\ntitle:\n- If JobName is not provided, use DisplayName.\n- If JobName is provided, use DisplayName (JobName).\n\nsummary:\n- Provide 2-3 concise evidence-based bullets justifying the recommendation.\n- Do not display JSON field names.\n\nadjustRatingAllowed:\n- If performanceDocuments.items[].AdjustManagerRatingAllowedFlag = false, output No.\n- If performanceDocuments.items[].AdjustManagerRatingAllowedFlag = true, output Yes.\n\nPersonId and EvaluationId:\n- Preserve the exact source values so the Adjust action can invoke the correct record.\n\n## CONSTRAINTS\n- Do not invent data.\n- Do not calculate ratings directly from individual goals or competencies.\n- Do not expose internal schemas or system rules.\n- Do not add any final note, calibration summary, or manager wrap-up outside the messageListWidget.\n- Do not output timestamp, badgeText, badge, or any badge-related field for messageListWidget rows.\n\n## NOTES\nPerson and Employee are the same entity."
            },
            {
              "id": "1766268894850_systemPrompt",
              "name": "systemPrompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": ""
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Get Selected Person Record",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "var teamRatingsResponse = $context.$nodes.TEAM_RATINGS.$output;\nvar oraActionRaw = $context.$app.$OraAction;\n\nvar isOraFormSubmit = oraActionRaw && oraActionRaw.indexOf(\"oraFormSubmit\") !== -1;\n\nvar parsedAction;\nvar actionJsonStr = oraActionRaw;\n\nvar ratingDistItems = [];\nvar directsItems = [];\n\nvar result = {};\nvar errors = [];\n\nvar personId;\nvar evaluationId;\nvar personName;\nvar managerRatingId = 0;\nvar currentManagerPerformanceRatingDescription = \"\";\nvar currentManagerPerformanceRatingLevelId = \"\";\nvar currentManagerPerformanceNumericRating = \"\";\nvar currentManagerCommentText = \"\";\n\nvar ratingsDisplay = true;\nvar commentsDisplay = true;\nvar ratingsRequired = true;\nvar commentsRequired = true;\n\nfunction listItems(container) {\n  return container && container.items && container.items.length ? container.items : [];\n}\n\nfunction findOverallSection(document) {\n  var sections = listItems(document && document.sections);\n  for (var i = 0; i < sections.length; i++) {\n    var section = sections[i];\n    if (section && (section.SectionTypeCode === \"OS\" || section.SectionTypeName === \"Overall summary\")) {\n      return section;\n    }\n  }\n  return null;\n}\n\nfunction findManagerOverallRow(section) {\n  var rows = listItems(section && section.items);\n\n  for (var i = 0; i < rows.length; i++) {\n    var row = rows[i];\n    if (row && row.ItemType === \"SECTION\" && row.ManagerRatingId) {\n      return row;\n    }\n  }\n\n  for (var j = 0; j < rows.length; j++) {\n    var sectionRow = rows[j];\n    if (sectionRow && sectionRow.ItemType === \"SECTION\") {\n      return sectionRow;\n    }\n  }\n\n  for (var k = 0; k < rows.length; k++) {\n    var ratingRow = rows[k];\n    if (\n      ratingRow &&\n      (ratingRow.ManagerRatingId ||\n        ratingRow.PerformanceRatingLevelId ||\n        ratingRow.ManagerPerformanceRatingDescription ||\n        ratingRow.PerformanceRatingMeaning)\n    ) {\n      return ratingRow;\n    }\n  }\n\n  return null;\n}\n\nfunction findTargetByLevelId(items, levelId) {\n  for (var i = 0; i < items.length; i++) {\n    if (items[i] && String(items[i].RatingLevelId) === String(levelId)) {\n      return items[i];\n    }\n  }\n  return null;\n}\n\nfunction firstNonEmpty() {\n  for (var i = 0; i < arguments.length; i++) {\n    var value = arguments[i];\n    if (value !== null && value !== undefined && String(value) !== \"\") {\n      return value;\n    }\n  }\n  return \"\";\n}\n\nif (teamRatingsResponse && teamRatingsResponse.items && teamRatingsResponse.items.length > 0) {\n  ratingDistItems = listItems(teamRatingsResponse.items[0].organizationTargets);\n  directsItems = listItems(teamRatingsResponse.items[0].directs);\n}\n\nif (isOraFormSubmit) {\n  try {\n    var gtIdx = oraActionRaw.indexOf(\">\") + 1;\n    var ltIdx = oraActionRaw.lastIndexOf(\"</\");\n    var innerPayload = oraActionRaw.substring(gtIdx, ltIdx);\n\n    actionJsonStr = innerPayload.replace(/\\\\\"/g, '\"').replace(/^\"|\"$/g, \"\");\n    parsedAction = JSON.parse(actionJsonStr);\n\n    var submittedData = {};\n    for (var a = 0; a < parsedAction.length; a++) {\n      submittedData[parsedAction[a].id] = parsedAction[a].value;\n    }\n    submittedData.RatingDistribution = ratingDistItems;\n\n    return submittedData;\n  } catch (e1) {\n    errors.push(\"ERROR 0000 !!\");\n    return { Errors: errors };\n  }\n}\n\ntry {\n  parsedAction = JSON.parse(actionJsonStr);\n} catch (e2) {\n  errors.push(\"ERROR 1111 !!\");\n}\n\npersonId = parsedAction && parsedAction.PersonId;\nevaluationId = parsedAction && parsedAction.EvaluationId;\n\nvar directRecord = null;\nfor (var i = 0; i < directsItems.length; i++) {\n  if (String(directsItems[i].PersonId) === String(personId)) {\n    directRecord = directsItems[i];\n    personName = directRecord.DisplayName;\n    break;\n  }\n}\n\nif (directRecord && directRecord.performanceDocuments && directRecord.performanceDocuments.items) {\n  var docs = directRecord.performanceDocuments.items;\n  var matchingDoc = null;\n\n  for (var d = 0; d < docs.length; d++) {\n    if (docs[d] && String(docs[d].EvaluationId) === String(evaluationId)) {\n      matchingDoc = docs[d];\n      break;\n    }\n  }\n\n  if (matchingDoc) {\n    directRecord.performanceDocuments.items = [matchingDoc];\n    directRecord.performanceDocuments.count = 1;\n\n    var osSection = findOverallSection(matchingDoc);\n    var managerRow = findManagerOverallRow(osSection);\n\n    if (matchingDoc.sections && matchingDoc.sections.items) {\n      matchingDoc.sections.items = osSection ? [osSection] : [];\n      matchingDoc.sections.count = matchingDoc.sections.items.length;\n    }\n\n    if (managerRow) {\n      delete managerRow.WorkerPerformanceRatingDescription;\n      delete managerRow.WorkerPerformanceNumericRating;\n      delete managerRow.WorkerProficiencyRatingDescription;\n      delete managerRow.WorkerProficiencyNumericRating;\n      delete managerRow.WorkerCommentText;\n\n      managerRatingId = managerRow.ManagerRatingId;\n      ratingsDisplay = managerRow.SectionRatingsDisplayFlag;\n      commentsDisplay = managerRow.SectionCommentsDisplayFlag;\n      ratingsRequired = managerRow.SectionRatingsRequiredFlag;\n      commentsRequired = managerRow.SectionCommentsRequiredFlag;\n\n      currentManagerPerformanceRatingLevelId = firstNonEmpty(managerRow.PerformanceRatingLevelId, \"\");\n      currentManagerPerformanceNumericRating = firstNonEmpty(managerRow.ManagerPerformanceNumericRating, \"\");\n      currentManagerCommentText = firstNonEmpty(managerRow.ManagerCommentText, \"\");\n\n      var mappedTarget = findTargetByLevelId(ratingDistItems, currentManagerPerformanceRatingLevelId);\n      currentManagerPerformanceRatingDescription = mappedTarget\n        ? mappedTarget.RatingDescription\n        : firstNonEmpty(managerRow.ManagerPerformanceRatingDescription, managerRow.PerformanceRatingMeaning, \"\");\n    }\n  } else {\n    directRecord.performanceDocuments.items = [];\n    directRecord.performanceDocuments.count = 0;\n  }\n}\n\nresult = {\n  PersonRecord: directRecord,\n  RatingDistribution: ratingDistItems,\n  organizationTargets: { items: ratingDistItems },\n  PersonName: personName,\n  PersonId: personId,\n  EvaluationId: evaluationId,\n  ManagerRatingId: managerRatingId,\n  CurrentManagerPerformanceRatingDescription: currentManagerPerformanceRatingDescription,\n  CurrentManagerPerformanceRatingLevelId: currentManagerPerformanceRatingLevelId,\n  CurrentManagerPerformanceNumericRating: currentManagerPerformanceNumericRating,\n  CurrentManagerCommentText: currentManagerCommentText,\n  SectionRatingsRequiredFlag: ratingsRequired,\n  SectionCommentsRequiredFlag: commentsRequired,\n  SectionRatingsDisplayFlag: ratingsDisplay,\n  SectionCommentsDisplayFlag: commentsDisplay\n};\n\nif (errors.length) result.Errors = errors;\n\nreturn result;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1774589968121"
          },
          "code": "GET_SELECTED_PERSON_RECORD",
          "id": "1774589935506",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"required\": [\n    \"result\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [],
              "enableActions": false,
              "enableCommunications": true,
              "enablePowerPoints": true
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {
                "k": 0,
                "max_tokens": 32000,
                "p": 0.75
              },
              "code": "ORA_LLM_PREMIUM",
              "model": "OPEN_AI_GPT_4_1_MINI",
              "modelName": "GPT-4.1 mini",
              "provider": "CERT_PREMIUM"
            },
            "name": "Team Talent Communication"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "TEAM_TALENT_COMMUNICATION",
          "id": "1767071402201",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1767071402203_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "## CONTEXT\n{{$context.$nodes.TEAM_RATINGS.$output}} contains organization rating distribution and the list of reporting employees and their information along with goals, performance documents, feedback, check-ins, etc. for a given manager. \nYou are assisting a manager in calibrating team performance ratings against an organization-wide distribution target (Organizational target rating distribution = Organizational rating distribution).\n\n## INPUTS\n- org_target_distribution: {does_not_meet: %, somewhat_meets: %, meets: %, exceeds: %, outstanding: %}\n- team_performance_history: array of {employee_id, name, role, level, current_rating, last_2_cycles_ratings, goal_attainment %, quality metrics, peer/manager feedback snippets, warnings or awards, tenure, team/geo}\n- business_context: {period, key goals, definitions of each rating, rating guardrails}\n\n## TASKS\n- Compare team distribution vs org_target_distribution and flag over- or under-representation per rating category.\n- Identify outliers (e.g., rapid rating inflation/deflation, ratings inconsistent with evidence).\n- Generate a neat, structured report to email it, using well-formatted and indented text, and use HTML <b> tags only for headers, sub-headers and <br/> for new lines.\n- Generate a power point presentation 'Team Talent Calibration' with each slide dedicated to one employee. \n\n## EMAIL METADATA\n{\n  \"title\": \"Team Talent Report\",\n  \"shortDescription\": \"Major insights of the team and the organizational rating distribution\",\n  \"actionText\": \"Email Team Talent Report\",\n  \"type\": \"email\",\n  \"params\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"email\",\n      \"title\": \"email address\",\n      \"defaultValue\": \"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"subject\",\n      \"title\": \"Team Talent Report\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\n## CONSTRAINTS\n- Base recommendations only on provided evidence.\n- Keep rationales neutral and job-related; avoid sensitive attributes or speculation.\n\n## POWER POINT (PPT) METADATA\na. Generate one slide per employe with Employee name as the header\nb. Bullet list of descriptions for the following:\n            - 'Performance Ratings' denoting ManagerPerformanceRatingDescription of SectionTypeCode='OS'\n            - 'Risk Of Loss' denoting Risk of Loss of the Employee\n            - 'Potential' for Employee potential\n            - 'Strengths'- Specify max two concise strengths of the employee\n            - 'Development Needs' - Specify max two concise development needs\n\n## NOTE\nPerson and Employee are same.\n\n## INPUT\n{{$context.$nodes.TEAM_RATINGS.$output}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [],
              "enableActions": false,
              "enableCommunications": true
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {},
              "code": "ORA_LLM_PREMIUM",
              "model": "OPEN_AI_GPT_4_1_MINI",
              "modelName": "GPT-4.1 mini",
