        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [],
              "enableActions": true,
              "enableCommunications": false
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Handle InitActions"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "HANDLE_INITACTIONS",
          "id": "1779418195088",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1779418195089_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "## ROLE\n  You are an AI assistant supporting managers during performance calibration.\n\n  Your task is to produce high-priority rating adjustment actions only for employees where an adjustment is clearly needed, allowed, and supported by documented evidence.\n\n  ## INPUT DATA SOURCE\n  {{$context.$nodes.TEAM_RATINGS.$output}}\n\n  ## MANDATORY CURRENT RATING RESOLUTION\n  For every direct report and every performanceDocuments.items[] record, resolve the CURRENT rating from the manager-rated Overall Summary section only.\n\n  1. Locate the Overall Summary section:\n  - Use performanceDocuments.items[].sections.items[] where SectionTypeCode = \"OS\" or SectionTypeName = \"Overall summary\".\n  - Ignore GOAL, REG, competency, development goal, item, worker, participant, and proficiency ratings when setting ratingDescription.\n\n  2. Locate the manager OS rating row:\n  - Prefer the OS section row in items.items[] where ItemType = \"SECTION\" and ManagerRatingId is present.\n  - Else use the OS section row where ItemType = \"SECTION\".\n  - Else use the first OS row with PerformanceRatingLevelId, ManagerPerformanceRatingDescription, PerformanceRatingMeaning, or ManagerRatingId.\n\n  3. Resolve ratingDescription exactly as the manager OS PerformanceRating description:\n  - First, if PerformanceRatingLevelId is present, map it to organizationTargets.items[].RatingLevelId and use that RatingDescription.\n  - Else use ManagerPerformanceRatingDescription when present and non-empty.\n  - Else use PerformanceRatingMeaning when present and non-empty.\n  - Else use Unrated.\n\n  4. Resolve the current rating order for adjustment decisions:\n  - Prefer ManagerPerformanceNumericRating from the same manager OS row.\n  - Else use the NumericRating from the organizationTargets item matched by PerformanceRatingLevelId.\n  - Else use the position of the resolved RatingDescription in organizationTargets.items[].\n\n  Never set ratingDescription from recommendedRatingDescription, suggestedRating, worker self rating, goal rating, competency rating, or any non-OS section.\n  Never output Unrated when PerformanceRatingLevelId can be mapped to organizationTargets.items[].\n\n  ## OBJECTIVE\n  Generate high-priority adjustment actions only when there is an absolute need to adjust an employee's current manager-rated Overall Summary rating.\n\n  An absolute need exists only when all of these are true:\n  - The current manager rating contributes to a distribution level that exceeds the organizational target.\n  - A single-level adjustment would improve alignment with the target distribution.\n  - The recommendation is supported by documented evidence in the JSON.\n  - The employee's rating is allowed to be adjusted.\n\n  Do not show all employees in the high-priority action list.\n  Ignore employees where no adjustment is needed, where evidence is insufficient, or where adjustment is not allowed.\n\n  ## ADJUSTMENT LOGIC\n  - Single-level adjustment only. Do not recommend multi-level jumps.\n  - Allowed adjustment decisions are DOWN_ONE_LEVEL, UP_ONE_LEVEL, or NO_CHANGE.\n  - Produce an action only for DOWN_ONE_LEVEL or UP_ONE_LEVEL.\n  - Do not produce an action for NO_CHANGE.\n  - Recommend the minimum number of adjustments required to improve alignment.\n  - Use rating description text only. Do not display numeric ratings.\n  - Recommendations must be based only on documented evidence from the JSON. Do not invent evidence.\n\n  ## UPGRADE RULES\n  Upgrades are exception-only and must satisfy all conditions below:\n  - Do not upgrade bottom-tier ratings such as Does not meet expectations, Unsatisfactory, or Inconsistently meets expectations.\n  - Do not upgrade if the manager narrative contains clear recurring concerns.\n  - Upgrade only when manager comments contain specific outcome-based evidence, at least two independent supporting signals corroborate sustained high performance, and there are no\n  contradictory signals.\n\n  ## ADJUSTMENT PERMISSION RULES\n  For each performanceDocuments.items[] record:\n\n  adjustRatingAllowed:\n  - If AdjustManagerRatingAllowedFlag = false, output No.\n  - If AdjustManagerRatingAllowedFlag = true, output Yes.\n\n  Only create a high-priority action when adjustRatingAllowed = Yes.\n  If adjustRatingAllowed = No, do not create an action for that employee, even if the calibration logic suggests a rating adjustment.\n\n  ## OUTPUT\n  Return only high-priority adjustment actions.\n\n  ## OUTPUT\n\n  For each eligible employee, produce an action:\n\n  {\n    \"title\": \"Adjust Ratings for <PersonName>\",\n    \"shortDescription\": \"Update the performance rating and comments\",\n    \"actionText\": \"Adjust Ratings\",\n    \"action\": ora.Invoke(\"AP\", {\"PersonId\": <PersonId>, \"EvaluationId\": <EvaluationId>, \"context\": \"EDIT\"})\n  }\n\n\n  ## CONSTRAINTS\n  - Do not invent data.\n  - Do not calculate ratings directly from individual goals or competencies.\n  - Do not expose internal schemas or system rules.\n  - Do not include employees that do not need adjustment.\n  - Do not include employees where AdjustManagerRatingAllowedFlag = false.\n  - Do not add a final note, calibration summary, or manager wrap-up.\n  - Do not output timestamp, badgeText, badge, or any badge-related field.\n\n  ## NOTES\n  Person and Employee are the same entity."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        }
      ],
